@page "/privacy"
@namespace Parrot.Web.Components.Pages.Legal
@using Parrot.Web.Components.Layout.Landing
@layout LandingPageLayout

@* The reviewed Privacy Policy (designer, 23 November 2026), effective 19 November 2026. Only these changes from the
   document as received, each the designer's call: the product is "yára" (it said "YARA CRM"), TikTok is named with the
   other channels, the company is LandingCompany.Name, and the deletion and contact email is LandingCompany.Email (it
   said "[Insert official privacy email]"). Long sentences that list several things are shown as lists. *@
<LandingMetadata Title="Privacy Policy · yára" Description="How yára collects, uses, stores, shares and protects personal information, and how to ask for your data to be accessed, corrected or deleted." Path="/privacy" />

<LandingDocument Title="Privacy Policy" Effective="new DateOnly(2026, 11, 19)" Updated="new DateOnly(2026, 11, 19)">
    <LandingSection Title="1. Introduction">
        <p>yára is an AI-powered customer relationship management and business communication platform associated with @LandingCompany.Name. We help businesses manage customer conversations, automate workflows, and engage customers across supported channels, including WhatsApp, Facebook Messenger, Instagram and TikTok.</p>
        <p>This policy explains how we collect, use, store, share, and protect personal information in accordance with applicable data protection laws, including the Nigeria Data Protection Act, 2023.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="2. Information we collect">
        <p>We may collect:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>business account and contact details;</li>
            <li>customer names, phone numbers, and profiles;</li>
            <li>messages, attachments, and conversation histories;</li>
            <li>technical data such as IP addresses, device information, and security logs; and</li>
            <li>information provided through authorized third-party integrations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The information processed depends on the services and permissions enabled.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="3. How we use information">
        <p>We use information to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>provide CRM and messaging services;</li>
            <li>enable authorized WhatsApp, Facebook, Instagram and TikTok integrations;</li>
            <li>support AI-powered assistance and automated workflows;</li>
            <li>manage inquiries, appointments, sales, and follow-ups;</li>
            <li>maintain security and reliability; and</li>
            <li>comply with legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We rely on appropriate legal grounds, including contract, consent, legitimate interests, and legal obligations, as applicable. We do not sell personal information or use Meta platform data for unauthorized purposes.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="4. Third-party integrations">
        <p>Businesses may connect authorized WhatsApp Business Platform, Facebook Messenger, Instagram and TikTok accounts. We may process account identifiers, customer information, messages, and delivery statuses as needed to provide requested services.</p>
        <p>Businesses are responsible for required customer permissions and compliance with applicable messaging policies. Third-party platforms also have their own privacy practices. References to these platforms do not imply endorsement.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="5. AI-powered services">
        <p>When enabled, AI features may process relevant messages, conversation context, and authorized business information to support replies and automated tasks. Where third-party AI providers are used, appropriate contractual and privacy safeguards should apply.</p>
        <p>Businesses remain responsible for appropriate oversight of customer-facing automated interactions.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="6. Sharing and security">
        <p>We may share necessary information with authorized cloud hosting, messaging, AI, payment, technical support, and security providers, or with authorities where legally required.</p>
        <p>We apply appropriate safeguards, including access controls and secure authentication, to protect personal data. No digital system can guarantee absolute security.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="7. Data retention and deletion">
        <p>We retain information only as long as needed to deliver services, meet contractual requirements, or satisfy legal obligations.</p>
        <p>Subject to applicable law, individuals may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability, or withdrawal of consent where relevant.</p>
        <p>To request deletion, email <a href="mailto:@(LandingCompany.Email)?subject=Data%20Deletion%20Request">@LandingCompany.Email</a> with the subject “Data Deletion Request.” We verify and process valid requests under applicable law. Where a business controls customer data, we may direct requests to that business or assist it. See also <a href="/data-deletion">Delete your data</a>.</p>
        <p>Disconnecting an integration stops corresponding authorized access but does not necessarily erase previously stored records.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="8. Cookies and international transfers">
        <p>We may use cookies and similar technologies for authentication, security, and platform functionality. Where personal information is processed outside Nigeria, we apply safeguards required by applicable data protection laws.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="9. Policy updates">
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy as our services or legal obligations change. Revisions will be published on our website with an updated date.</p>
    </LandingSection>
    <LandingSection Title="10. Contact us">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Website</strong>: <a href="@LandingCompany.SiteUrl">yarahq.com</a></li>
            <li><strong>Email</strong>: <a href="mailto:@LandingCompany.Email">@LandingCompany.Email</a></li>
            <li><strong>Address</strong>: @LandingCompany.Name, @LandingCompany.Address</li>
        </ul>
    </LandingSection>
</LandingDocument>
